<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 99,080 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 99,080 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 99,080 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Saturday, compared to 55,623 tonnes on Friday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Saturday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			86,782	    41,964</p>
<p>    Import cargo			12,298	    13,659</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, 11 ships are expected to sail and 12 to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Chemical		  2,000	Bow Arrow		 due</p>
<p>Chemical		 10,000	San Mateo		 due</p>
<p>General cargo	   7,702	Ivan Zegubanski	 27/4</p>
<p>Rock phosphate	 22,000	Artemis II		27/4</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
